3847: # ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- reviewer roster
3848: #
3849: # The reviewer roster is an ordered list of reviewers the operator is willing to use, first
3850: # choice first. A JSON file (never created by the bridge):
3851: #   CODEX_CONSULT_ROSTER=<path>   that file; it MUST exist (a roster that is asked for and
3852: #                                 missing refuses the run - it is never skipped silently)
3853: #   CODEX_CONSULT_ROSTER=none     no roster at all, the default file is ignored too
3854: #   unset                         <codex home>/codex-consult-roster.json when it exists;
3855: #                                 absent = no roster: everything behaves as without one
3856: #
3857: #   { "roster_version": 1,
3858: #     "reviewers": [ { "provider": "openai", "model": "gpt-5.1" },
3859: #                    { "provider": "ZAI", "model": "glm-5.3" },
3860: #                    { "provider": "local", "model": "m", "auth": "none",
3861: #                      "codex_config": ["model_catalog_json=~/.codex/catalog.json"] } ] }
3862: #
3863: #   provider      required: a [model_providers.<name>] table of the Codex config
3864: #                 (case-sensitive) or openai
3865: #   model         optional: absent = the model resolves as without a roster (the Codex
3866: #                 config's top-level model)
3867: #   codex_config  optional: key=value items with exactly the -CodexConfig rules
3868: #                 (ConvertFrom-CodexConfigItems)
3869: #   auth          optional, only "none": the endpoint needs no credential (a table without
3870: #                 env_key/bearer token then passes the credential check; a table WITH
3871: #                 env_key still needs the variable)
3872: #   panel         optional, "always" (the default) or "weighty": with -Panel a weighty
3873: #                 reviewer joins only on the weighty purposes (framing, decision,
3874: #                 core-contract, acceptance, stuck) or with -PanelAll. The single-reviewer
3875: #                 walk ignores it.
3876: #   engine        optional (0.4.0), "codex" (the default) or "agy": the CLI that carries the
3877: #                 consultation. For agy the provider is a free label (the lineage's
3878: #                 provider, e.g. "gemini"), the model is REQUIRED (the full id with its
3879: #                 tier), codex_config and auth are refused, and one label names one engine
3880: #                 across the roster. Two entries with the same label and different models
3881: #                 are fine (e.g. a "panel": "weighty" entry on the pro model).
3882: #   parallel      optional TOP-LEVEL object (0.4.x wave 21) { "<provider label>": <n> }: a
3883: #                 -Panel runs the members of one endpoint one after another (Get-PanelPlan);
3884: #                 n >= 1 lets that label's members run n at a time. Every key must be a
3885: #                 label the roster uses, every value an integer >= 1.
3886: # Anything else - an unknown key, roster_version other than 1, reviewers not an array or
3887: # empty, the same (provider, model) twice, a file that does not parse - makes the roster
3888: # unusable, and the bridge refuses to run (fail-closed: an existing roster is never
3889: # ignored).
3890: #
3891: # Selection (codex-consult.ps1; codex-providers.ps1 shows the same walk):
3892: #   -Provider given   the roster does not select; the first entry of that provider (by
3893: #                     -Model too when several entries name it) supplies its model when
3894: #                     -Model is empty and its codex_config when -CodexConfig is empty
3895: #   -Thread given     the thread's ledger entry fixes the reviewer; its roster entry
3896: #                     supplies codex_config
3897: #   otherwise         the roster is walked in order and the first entry whose preflight is
3898: #                     available is used (Select-RosterReviewer); every skipped entry is
3899: #                     recorded with its reason. None available: refused.
3900: #   -Panel            every available entry (Select-PanelMembers) runs the same brief, each
3901: #                     as a consultation of its own; members of different endpoints at once,
3902: #                     of one endpoint one after another (Get-PanelPlan, roster "parallel").
3903: 
3904: # Where the roster comes from: { Path ('' when none); FromEnv (CODEX_CONSULT_ROSTER named
3905: # it: it must exist); Disabled (CODEX_CONSULT_ROSTER=none) }.
